  "body": "## Issue\nRefs #714 (left: part 3, the profile prefetch, waits on the Mac capture #716)\nClaim: cloud/i714-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5\n\n## What and why\nOperator device feedback: an MP row shows initials when the cache has no avatar, even for a correspondent who has one. Parts 1, 2, 4 of #714.\n\n- **Cause:** `AvatarCache` names files by the hex of the pseudo; the legacy app's files sit in the same folder as `MD5(lowercased pseudo)` (`MPListView.swift:911-917`, writer `ParseMessagesOperation.m:340-347` @ `87fe0d1c`), so after the update from legacy every cached avatar was ignored.\n- **Part 1:** `AvatarCache.entryAdoptingLegacy(forPseudo:accepting:)`: no entry → read the legacy file (read-only; regular file by `attributesOfItem`, which does not follow a link; ≤ 256 KiB; the app's `accepting` closure checks it decodes as an image), copy it under the SwiftHFR name keeping its date. MD5 is a small RFC 1321 function in the engine (`LegacyAvatarName`: Foundation-only, no CryptoKit on Linux, no dependency). A pseudo with U+200B is tried as printed (legacy) and stripped (ours).\n- **Part 2:** `MessageRowView.avatarSubject(of:)`: one-to-one → the interlocutor (the list's starter cell, never the account's pseudo), trimmed as legacy; group → icon. Difference from legacy: only the whole label \"Interlocuteurs multiples\" counts as a group, not any pseudo containing \"multiples\".\n- **Part 4:** unchanged fallback: no entry or a failed read → monogram.\n- Spec: LOT-066 updated.\n\n## How it was verified\n- Engine (`swift test`, run here): `LegacyAvatarAdoptionTests` (RFC 1321 vectors, adoption + legacy file untouched + date kept, existing entry wins, ZWSP spellings, not-an-image / empty / over-cap / missing, symlink and directory refused, unsafe folder throws). New API, so the suite cannot compile without the change; the symlink guard test fails with the guard removed (checked).\n- App (`MessageRowAvatarTests`, parser rows of captures R13u1 and R123a): not run here (Linux), reviewed with compiler rigour.\n- **Mac check:** install over a legacy install with cached avatars: the MP list shows the correspondents' avatars at once; a member without avatar shows initials; a group shows its icon.\n\n## Ledger\n```gap-edit\nGAP-230\nSwiftHFR final: `AvatarStore` fills the cache from every page read (cookie-less, forum image host only, 256 KiB cap, 24 h; not gated by \"Images externes\": forum avatars are first-party (LOT-071 D-071-1 point 3), as in the reader and legacy); the avatar files the legacy app cached (`MD5(lowercased pseudo)`) are adopted on first read after an update (#714); monogram (initials, stable hue, ≥ 4.5:1) replaces the grey disc when there is none; groups keep their icon. Profile prefetch for never-opened correspondents: pending capture (#716).\nLot/Feat: LOT-126, LOT-066, #569, #714\n```\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Module boundaries respected; no UI framework in HFRKit\n- [x] Tests added (engine run, app reviewed)\n- [x] No secrets; synthetic pseudos\n- [x] Docs updated (LOT-066)\n- [ ] Author model: Sonnet 5.5 / Reviewer model: Opus (pending)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CGVtTL2tepawhCcYoK)_",
