   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 5624843 (reviewer's report, verbatim)\n\n1. **High**: `LegacyAvatarName.swift:41`. `md5(_:)` has cyclomatic complexity 11, over the limit of 10. CI runs `swiftlint lint --strict` (ci.yml:28, 0.65.1), which turns that warning into an error. Fix: add `cyclomatic_complexity` to the justified `swiftlint:disable`.\n2. **Low**: `MessageRowAvatarTests.swift:16-38`. `capturedRows` and `everyRow` would also pass with the old inline expression (every group row in R13u1/R123a has a tooltip, so `isGroup` is already true). Only `normalisation` and `multiplesLabel` fail without the change.\n3. **Low**: `AvatarCache.swift:100-105`. TOCTOU: the type check and `Data(contentsOf:)` are two opens; a link swapped in between would be followed. Risk minimal (only code inside the sandbox writes there). Fix: open once with O_NOFOLLOW + fstat, or document.\n4. **Detail**: `AvatarCache.swift:26`: `cache` went from `private` to internal for nothing; restore `private`.\n5. **Detail**: `MessageAvatarView.swift:5`: the `@ 2440d79` pointer was rewritten; keep it and add the new one next to it.\n\nVerified by the reviewer: 18/18 engine tests pass (RFC 1321 vectors incl. a 2-block input); mutation (type check removed) fails the symlink test; MD5 name and folder match legacy `MPListView.swift:911-917`, `ParseMessagesOperation.m:340-347` @ 87fe0d1c; R13u1 rows end with U+200B, both spellings tried; `avatarSubject` correct on R13u1/R123a; no ledger/GAP file touched.\n\nAuthor response (fix in d3e796d + follow-up): 1 fixed; 2 accepted, said here (the two parser-row tests pin the current behaviour, the other two cover the change); 3 documented as accepted gap in the code; 4 fixed; 5 fixed.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
