   "body": "**Adversarial re-check (Opus 5.5): APPROVE** — head `2cf59f057fd06eb50900950628b5925cc2f04a8c` (reviewer's report, condensed verbatim)\n\nRound-1 findings rechecked: (1) fixed, `cyclomatic_complexity` added to the scoped disable, `swiftlint --strict` on the 6 changed files: 0 violations; (2) accepted; (3) TOCTOU documented as accepted gap; (4) `cache` is `private` again; (5) both legacy pointers (`@ 2440d79`, `@ 87fe0d1c :911-917`) present, checked at both commits.\nTests: `swift test --filter \"AvatarCache|LegacyAvatarAdoption\"` 18/18. Whole diff: no new blocking problem (256 KiB cap equals `AnonymousAvatarLoader.maximumBytes`; `AvatarImage.isDecodable` exists; too-long pseudo / unsafe folder throw before any legacy read and the view swallows it; adopted copy keeps the legacy date; concurrent adoptions safe, `store` is atomic).\nNit (non-blocking, cosmetic): re-flow the pointer comment at `MessageAvatarView.swift:5-8` next time the file is touched.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
